    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, led by **Tyler Soderstrom**, who paces our lineup with a 72.72 efficiency score. **Soderstrom** benefits from a prime matchup against a soft Meibrys Kelly (5.31 xERA), and his promotion to the #2 spot amplifies his fantasy footprint. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (69.85) and **James Wood** (69.19) are must-starts today; **Moniak** leverages a massive +14% park factor, while **Wood** remains an engine for our offense, boasting an elite 0.425 xwOBA that makes his lead-off role against Hughes incredibly valuable. **Vinnie Pasquantino** also projects exceptionally well at 67.63, driven by a +14% platoon edge against Roupp, providing us with a high-floor anchor in the UTIL spot.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Naylor**, whose 59.33 score nearly pushed him into the starting nine. Ultimately, **Naylor** was benched due to a combination of a poor park factor (-5%) and a significant negative BvP history, which forced the optimizer to favor the higher-upside profiles of **Isaac Paredes** and **Jose Caballero**. While we are keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley**, his 64.88 score is currently threatened by a 35% rain risk; should his game face a delay, we are prepared to pivot to our deeper bench reserves. We are also monitoring the confirmed lineups for **Dalton Rushing**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Austin Riley**, and **Seiya Suzuki**, as their scores were calculated using assumed batting orders. With **Corbin Carroll** (58.95) providing essential stolen base upside despite a tougher matchup against Jump, the roster remains optimized to maximize our specific 5x5 category scarcity.",
